  "generating_specification": {
    "adstock": "Delayed geometric: w_l proportional to alpha**((l - theta)**2), normalised, which peaks at lag theta",
    "fitted_with": "Geometric adstock and logistic saturation. Geometric adstock is the generating kernel with theta pinned to zero, so it cannot represent a delayed peak at all, and a logistic curve cannot take the Hill shape. The mismatch is deliberate: a model fitted to data its own functional form produced recovers its own assumptions and measures nothing. The matched arm of the recovery grid separates misspecification error from identification error.",
